==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἴσος|tr=isos||equal|lang=grc}} + {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|χρόνος|tr=chrónos|sc=polytonic|lang=grc}} + {{term|-ous|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# happening at [[regular]] [[interval]]s
# happening at the same [[time]]; [[isochronal]]
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} of or pertaining to the use of clocks derived from the same clock reference
#: ''Their entire national telephone network is '''isochronous''', with a clock distribution tree radiating from a single, protected cesium reference clock.''
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} of or pertaining to data associated with time sensitive application
#: ''These packets belong to an '''isochronous''' voice application and need priority handling.''

